IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `er5-admin-coverage-decision`

-- Tests of er5-admin-coverage-decision (reg 88). Expected values are written by hand from the text of the Regulations
-- (SOR-96-332.txt lines 1668-1675), beside each assertion, before the run.

§ `Stages of a dispute`

-- A stage that was not taken, and stages taken with the day their decision becomes final.
`er5 test stage not taken` MEANS `er5 Stage of a dispute over a ruling` OF FALSE, NOTHING
`er5 test stage taken and not yet final` MEANS `er5 Stage of a dispute over a ruling` OF TRUE, NOTHING
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A `er5 Stage of a dispute over a ruling`
`er5 test stage taken and final on` MEANS `er5 Stage of a dispute over a ruling` OF TRUE, (JUST d)

§ `Reg 88(1)(a), (b) - the later of the days (src:1668-1674)`

-- (a) alone: the officer's ruling becomes final on January 10, 2020 and nothing is appealed.
#ASSERT `reg 88(1) the later of the day the officer's ruling becomes final and the day the decision at the last stage taken becomes final` (JUST (YMD 2020 1 10)) `er5 test stage not taken` `er5 test stage not taken` `er5 test stage not taken` `er5 test stage not taken` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2020 1 10)
-- (b)(i): an appeal to the Minister whose decision becomes final on March 5, 2020 is the later day.
#ASSERT `reg 88(1) the later of the day the officer's ruling becomes final and the day the decision at the last stage taken becomes final` (JUST (YMD 2020 1 10)) (`er5 test stage taken and final on` (YMD 2020 3 5)) `er5 test stage not taken` `er5 test stage not taken` `er5 test stage not taken` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2020 3 5)
-- (b)(ii): then the Tax Court of Canada, final on June 20, 2020.
#ASSERT `reg 88(1) the later of the day the officer's ruling becomes final and the day the decision at the last stage taken becomes final` (JUST (YMD 2020 1 10)) (`er5 test stage taken and final on` (YMD 2020 3 5)) (`er5 test stage taken and final on` (YMD 2020 6 20)) `er5 test stage not taken` `er5 test stage not taken` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2020 6 20)
-- (b)(iii) and (iv): all four stages taken; the last day of all is December 15, 2020.
#ASSERT `reg 88(1) the later of the day the officer's ruling becomes final and the day the decision at the last stage taken becomes final` (JUST (YMD 2020 1 10)) (`er5 test stage taken and final on` (YMD 2020 3 5)) (`er5 test stage taken and final on` (YMD 2020 6 20)) (`er5 test stage taken and final on` (YMD 2020 9 1)) (`er5 test stage taken and final on` (YMD 2020 12 15)) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2020 12 15)
-- The officer's ruling is not yet final: no day.
#ASSERT `reg 88(1) the later of the day the officer's ruling becomes final and the day the decision at the last stage taken becomes final` NOTHING `er5 test stage not taken` `er5 test stage not taken` `er5 test stage not taken` `er5 test stage not taken` EQUALS NOTHING
-- An appeal to the Minister has been made and is not yet decided with finality: no day.
#ASSERT `reg 88(1) the later of the day the officer's ruling becomes final and the day the decision at the last stage taken becomes final` (JUST (YMD 2020 1 10)) `er5 test stage taken and not yet final` `er5 test stage not taken` `er5 test stage not taken` `er5 test stage not taken` EQUALS NOTHING
-- A later stage is still open although the earlier one is final: no day.
#ASSERT `reg 88(1) the later of the day the officer's ruling becomes final and the day the decision at the last stage taken becomes final` (JUST (YMD 2020 1 10)) (`er5 test stage taken and final on` (YMD 2020 3 5)) `er5 test stage taken and not yet final` `er5 test stage not taken` `er5 test stage not taken` EQUALS NOTHING
-- "The later of": a stage whose day is earlier than the ruling's does not pull the answer back.
#ASSERT `reg 88(1) the later of the day the officer's ruling becomes final and the day the decision at the last stage taken becomes final` (JUST (YMD 2020 1 10)) (`er5 test stage taken and final on` (YMD 2020 1 5)) `er5 test stage not taken` `er5 test stage not taken` `er5 test stage not taken` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2020 1 10)
-- A stage that was not taken cannot lengthen the wait, whatever day is written beside it.
#ASSERT `reg 88(1) the later of the day the officer's ruling becomes final and the day the decision at the last stage taken becomes final` (JUST (YMD 2020 1 10)) `er5 test stage not taken` (`er5 Stage of a dispute over a ruling` OF FALSE, (JUST (YMD 2020 12 31))) `er5 test stage not taken` `er5 test stage not taken` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2020 1 10)

§ `Reg 88(2) - when subsection (1) does not apply (src:1675)`

#ASSERT `reg 88(2) subsection 88(1) does not apply` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 88(2) subsection 88(1) does not apply` FALSE)

§ `Reg 88(1) - the hour is not payable on the day (src:1668)`

-- The argument order is: a request has been made; the hour is one of the hours that is the subject of the ruling; the claimant qualifies on other hours; the day the later ruling becomes final; the day in question.
-- The later ruling becomes final on March 5, 2020: not payable on March 4.
#ASSERT `reg 88(1) no benefits are payable in respect of the hour on the day in question` TRUE TRUE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2020 3 5)) (YMD 2020 3 4)
-- On March 5 itself, the day the ruling becomes final, "until" is read as not before that day: payable (assumed, not ruled).
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 88(1) no benefits are payable in respect of the hour on the day in question` TRUE TRUE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2020 3 5)) (YMD 2020 3 5))
-- After it: payable.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 88(1) no benefits are payable in respect of the hour on the day in question` TRUE TRUE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2020 3 5)) (YMD 2020 3 6))
-- While some ruling is not yet final, there is no day, and benefits are not payable on any day.
#ASSERT `reg 88(1) no benefits are payable in respect of the hour on the day in question` TRUE TRUE FALSE NOTHING (YMD 2030 1 1)
-- No request for a ruling was made.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 88(1) no benefits are payable in respect of the hour on the day in question` FALSE TRUE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2020 3 5)) (YMD 2020 3 4))
-- The hour is not one of the hours that is the subject of the ruling.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 88(1) no benefits are payable in respect of the hour on the day in question` TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2020 3 5)) (YMD 2020 3 4))
-- Subsection (2): the claimant qualifies on other hours, so subsection (1) does not apply.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 88(1) no benefits are payable in respect of the hour on the day in question` TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST (YMD 2020 3 5)) (YMD 2020 3 4))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 88(1) no benefits are payable in respect of the hour on the day in question` TRUE TRUE TRUE NOTHING (YMD 2020 3 4))
